.TH ODYSSEY\-CTL 1 "2026" "odyssey-ctl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
odyssey\-ctl \- control a DDC/CI capable display from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odyssey\-ctl
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENT ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B odyssey\-ctl
reads and writes the OSD settings of a monitor over DDC/CI, the VESA MCCS
protocol carried on a display's DDC lines.
It was written for the Samsung Odyssey G5 (G53F) but works with any display
implementing MCCS 2.1.
.PP
The tool locates displays through
.IR /sys/class/drm ,
using the
.I ddc/i2c-dev
directory each connector exposes.
Internal panels do not provide one and are skipped.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List connected displays that expose a DDC bus.
.TP
.B info
Show the selected display's connector, bus and EDID identity.
.TP
.B features
List the features this tool knows about, with their VCP codes and named values.
.TP
.B caps
Dump the display's raw capability string.
.TP
.BI get " FEATURE"
Read a feature and print its current and maximum value.
.TP
.BI set " FEATURE VALUE"
Write a feature.
.I VALUE
is either a named value from
.B features
or a number.
.TP
.BI apply " [FILE]"
Write every setting listed in a profile.
Without
.IR FILE ,
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/odyssey-ctl/profile.conf
is used, falling back to
.IR ~/.config/odyssey-ctl/profile.conf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-display " " \fINAME\fR
Select a DRM connector, for example
.IR card1\-HDMI\-A\-1 .
Without this the first display found is used.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bus " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an i2c\-dev node directly, bypassing discovery.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-save
Ask the display to persist the change across a power cycle.
Some panels ignore the request.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Raise the log level.
May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH PROFILE FORMAT
A profile is a sequence of
.RI \(lq feature " = " value \(rq
lines using the names
.B features
prints.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
Unknown feature names and malformed values are reported and skipped.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/odyssey-ctl/profile.conf
Default profile applied by
.BR apply .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-odyssey-ctl.rules
Grants the
.B i2c
group access to DDC buses.
.SH NOTES
DDC/CI set requests are not acknowledged by the display, so a rejected value is
indistinguishable from success.
Read the feature back to confirm a change took effect.
.PP
The protocol is timing sensitive.
A display that has just woken up or is still training its link will NAK; the
tool retries three times before reporting failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Dim the panel:
.PP
.RS
.EX
odyssey\-ctl set brightness 40
.EE
.RE
.PP
Switch a specific display to DisplayPort:
.PP
.RS
.EX
odyssey\-ctl \-d card1\-HDMI\-A\-1 set input dp\-1
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcutil (1),
.BR drm (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by xRookieFight.
